  "plan": {
    "goal": "Size the binary .bed storage for a GWAS genotype dataset of 11579 samples and 8198693 variants, and report the per-chromosome .bed size for the largest chromosome.",
    "rationale": "The binary PLINK .bed format packs 2 bits per sample per variant (4 samples/byte). Total .bed size = n_samples × n_variants / 4 / 1e6 MB. Per-chromosome .bed size uses the same rule applied to the largest chromosome's variant count (1012095). The number of per-chromosome files equals the number of chromosomes in the reference build (24 for human: 22 autosomes + X + Y).",
